 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the penal law, in relation to enacting the \"Benny A. Lyde's\nUnarmed Act\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S7571",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7571-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §70.12, Pen L",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7571\n\nSPONSOR: HAMILTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the penal law, in relation to enacting\nthe \"Benny A. Lyde's Unarmed Act\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill allows for increased penalties for crimes against any individ-\nual convicted of a class B felony against an individual twenty-one years\nof age or younger. This serves as an additional measure to protect the\nyouth of New York against those who seek to do them harm.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends section two by adding section 70.12 requiring a minimum sentence\nof ten years, but no more than a sentence of thirty years for an indi-\nvidual convicted of a class B felony offense against an individual twen-\nty-one years of age or younger.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nUnder current law, New York does not haven an additional penalty for\nclass B felonies involving illegal weapon use against individual twen-\nty-one years of age or younger.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn amending, the penal law to include these provisions we set forth the\nstandard that violent felonies committed against the youth of New York\nare especially heinous and should be sentenced with the same severity.\nThere are no provisions under the current law that specifically protect\nthe youth from such egregious acts and it is a great injustice to the\nyouth of New York and a disservice to the communities that are tasked\nwith nurturing the youth. In addition the victims of these crimes have\nuntold potential that society will never know because it cut short\nbecause of these violent acts.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSome to the State because of increased sentences\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall become a law\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
